stop_token.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ stop_source: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
could not fully type-check
--
libstdc++ 13 <stop_token> converts without dropped bodies.  Fixed (round
163w): bits/semaphore_base.h:118 _M_try_acquire_until_impl (`struct
timespec' through <ctime>'s `using ::timespec',
cpp98_elaborated_type_specifier_finds_using_declaration) and the
__check_overflow instances of bits/atomic_timed_wait.h's `64us' and `4us'
(cpp11_user_defined_literal_call_forms).  Earlier fixed: the drop of
bits/atomic_wait.h:252 _S_for (cpp_functional_cast_through_typedef_
reinterprets).  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
